diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index b955a08..a84263c 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -39,3 +39,22 @@
 - `User#bot_limit_reached?` returns `false` for administrators and checks `created_bots.active.count >= Current.account.settings.bots_per_member` for members. Deactivated (deleted) bots do not count toward the limit, and lowering the limit leaves existing bots intact while blocking creation of new ones.
 - On `/bots` (`app/views/bots/index.html.erb`), when `Current.user.bot_limit_reached?` is true, the `"Add a chat bot"` link is omitted and a message stating the user has `"reached the limit"` is shown instead.
 - `BotsController` enforces `before_action :ensure_within_bot_limit, only: %i[ new create ]` returning `403 Forbidden` to block direct `GET /bots/new` and `POST /bots` attempts at or above the limit.
+
+## Moderation: Flood Protection, Webhook Failures & Suspension
+- **Suspension State on `User`**: Suspended bots remain `status: :active` (so they stay listed on `/bots`, retain their rooms/messages, and continue counting toward their owner's `bots_per_member` limit) and track suspension via `suspended_at` and `suspension_reason` (`User::Bot#suspended?`).
+- **Flooding Limits**:
+  - `User::Bot#attempt_message_post` uses a row lock (`with_lock`) to enforce a sliding 10-second window (`FLOOD_WINDOW_MICROSECONDS = 10_000_000`) stored in `users.recent_post_timestamps` (integer microseconds to avoid float rounding and SQLite `freeze_time` issues).
+  - Both `Rooms::BotMessagesController#create` (API posts) and `Bot::Webhook#handle_response` (webhook `200` replies) share `attempt_message_post`.
+  - Posting an 11th message within 10 seconds rejects the message and starts a 30-second cooldown (`cooldown_until`, `cooldown_attempts = 0`).
+  - During cooldown, `Rooms::BotMessagesController#create` responds with `429 Too Many Requests` and `Retry-After` (integer seconds remaining via `ceil`, minimum `1`), and webhook replies are not posted.
+  - Five more post attempts during the same cooldown suspend the bot (`Flooding: too many messages`). If the cooldown expires with fewer than 5 attempts, the next post clears the cooldown state.
+- **Webhook Failure Tracking**:
+  - `Bot::Webhook#deliver` wraps only `post_payload` in network/timeout exception handling. Any non-`2xx` response (`!response.is_a?(Net::HTTPSuccess)`), timeout, or connection error calls `bot.record_webhook_failure!`.
+  - Any `2xx` response calls `bot.record_webhook_success!` (resetting `webhook_failures_count` to `0`).
+  - Ten consecutive failed deliveries suspend the bot (`Failing webhooks: 10 consecutive failed deliveries`).
+- **Suspended Bot Enforcement**:
+  - `Rooms::BotMessagesController` returns `403 Forbidden` via `ensure_not_suspended` (before `set_room`).
+  - `Room#deliver_webhooks_later`, `Room#memberships.grant_to`, `Membership#deliver_joined_webhook_later`, `User#grant_membership_to_open_rooms`, and `Bot::Webhook#eligible?` all exclude suspended bots so no webhooks are enqueued or delivered.
+- **Administrator Reactivation**:
+  - `app/views/bots/_bot.html.erb` renders `"Suspended"` with `suspension_reason` for suspended bots, and renders a `"Reactivate"` button with `data-turbo-confirm` (native browser `confirm()`) only when `Current.user.administrator?`.
+  - `Bots::ReactivationsController#create` (`POST /bots/:bot_id/reactivation`) enforces `Current.user.administrator?` (`403 Forbidden` for non-admins) and calls `@bot.reactivate!`, which clears suspension, cooldown, recent post timestamps, and webhook failure counters.
